  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1100.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ed 1120.06 Parental Failure to Respond; Implementation of Changes by LEA",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1120.06 Parental Failure to Respond; Implementation of Changes by LEA.\n\n(a) If a parent fails to respond within 14 days after the sending of written prior notice pursuant to Ed 1120.04(b), the LEA shall implement its proposed changes if the LEA has taken reasonable measures to obtain informed written consent.\n\n(b) Reasonable measures shall include:\n\n(1) Documentation of telephone calls to the parent, made or attempted, and the results of those calls; and\n\n(2) Copies of correspondence sent to the parent and any responses received. Correspondence shall be sent certified mail, return receipt requested.\n\n(c) The processes provided for in Ed 1123 can be requested by either party at any time subject to the exceptions of Ed 1120.05(d) and (e).\n\nSource. (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ed 1100) #9197, eff 6-28-08; amd by #9812, eff 11-11-10; ss by #12141, eff 3-24-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1100.html"
